From dfc41b613c75ac3163cbf158e7dc8539fccdcb2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pixel3 port <pixel3@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:35:03 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] usb: typec: qcom-pmic-typec: add PMI8998 (SMB2) sink port
 backend

The PMI8998 has no TYPEC peripheral: CC detection is part of the USBIN
block of the SMB2 charger and runs in hardware. Its PD PHY however is the
same block as on PM8150B. Add a minimal sink-only port backend that
reports the hardware CC state/orientation and VBUS to TCPM, routes the
PD PHY to the active CC line (TYPEC_SPARE_CFG + VCONN_EN_ORIENTATION, as
the vendor driver does on PD activation), keeps the port attached across
VBUS drops (EXIT_SNK_BASED_ON_CC, needed for hard reset) and programs the
charger input current limit / 5-9 V adapter allowance from the
negotiated contract. Registers from the vendor smb-reg.h.

Signed-off-by: pixel3 port <pixel3@localhost>
